For any purpose, including commercially. These freedoms cannot be revoked so
long as you follow the terms below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
UNDER THE FOLLOWING TERMS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. ATTRIBUTION. You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the
   licence, and indicate if changes were made.

   The attribution line to reproduce:

     Zhongdex by SayMei — https://zhongdex.org — CC BY-SA 4.0.
     Contains data from CC-CEDICT (CC BY-SA 4.0), Wiktionary (CC BY-SA 4.0),
     and Tatoeba (CC BY 2.0 FR).

   Keep the per-record attribution that ships with the data. Sentence records
   carry `source.corpus` and, for Tatoeba rows, `source.sourceId`; that field
   IS the attribution for those rows and must survive your transformation.

2. SHAREALIKE. If you remix, transform, or build upon the material, you must
   distribute your contributions under CC BY-SA 4.0 or a
   ShareAlike-compatible licence.

   MIT and Apache-2.0 are NOT on Creative Commons' compatible-licence list.
   You cannot relicense this data under them.

   ShareAlike propagates through a merge: a database containing a substantial
   portion of this data is Adapted Material under §4 (sui generis database
   rights) and must itself be BY-SA.

   "Share" is defined by the licence as making the material available such
   that members of the public may access it from a place and at a time
   individually chosen by them. That definition covers an HTTP API and an MCP
   server exactly as it covers a download.

3. NO ADDITIONAL RESTRICTIONS. You may not apply legal terms or technological
   measures that legally restrict others from doing anything the licence
   permits.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS LICENCE, AND NOT A PERMISSIVE ONE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is not a preference. CC-CEDICT and Wiktionary are both CC BY-SA 4.0, and
their glosses are merged into the word canon. ShareAlike propagates through
that merge, so BY-SA is the only licence this corpus can carry. The code that
builds it is MIT (see ../LICENSE); the corpus cannot be.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT IS NOT COVERED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * The audio recordings. They are served from a separate host under their
    own terms, are referenced by URL and never bundled here, and AS OF v0.1
    ARE NOT PUBLISHED AT ALL — every audio field reports status "pending".
    See the README.
  * SayMei trademarks, the SayMei and Zhongdex names, and the logos. Licence
    terms do not grant trademark rights.
  * The build code in ../src, which is MIT.

